   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The double infinitive in past Konjunktiv II",
     "texto": [
      "When a modal verb (**können, müssen, sollen, dürfen, wollen**) is used in the past Konjunktiv II together with another verb in the infinitive, the modal doesn't take its participle but its own infinitive: this is the **double infinitive** (**Ersatzinfinitiv**) phenomenon:",
      "**Er hätte uns anrufen können** (he could have called us / he would have been able to call us).",
      "**Du hättest den Chef informieren müssen** (you should have informed the boss / you would have had to inform the boss).",
      "In main clauses, «hätte» goes in 2nd position and the two infinitives go at the end (first the lexical verb, last the modal: **anrufen können**).",
      "In subordinate clauses with **dass** or **weil**, the auxiliary «hätte» moves immediately in front of the double-infinitive block: **...weil er uns hätte anrufen können**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Modal",
